00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:08.150
So let's go right into
the market evolution.

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:13.790
What does it mean when ISVs
have to go into the cloud?

00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:16.260
There's some really
important implications.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:19.550
And it's much more
difficult than making sure

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:24.780
that your application
just runs on cloud xyz.

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:27.600
From the ISV side
of things, there's

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:32.430
more demands for the sales
motion from their customers.

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:35.370
Customers and
consumers in the cloud

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:39.840
are demanding more retail
consumer-like experiences.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:42.270
Because, quite
frankly, enterprises

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:46.110
don't care about what's actually
making the solution run.

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:48.940
They just want to have it work.

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:53.170
Pricing models, due to that
consumer focus that the cloud

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:56.560
is bringing, are moving more
towards consumption-based

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:57.950
models--

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:02.150
"pay by the sip", rather
than "pay by the drink".

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:05.000
We're also seeing
that making sure

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:08.990
that ISV systems can handle the
new monetization and pricing

00:03:08.990 --> 00:03:14.100
models in the cloud
can be difficult.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:17.130
And users are really
adopting cloud marketplaces

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:20.940
to browse different kinds of
solutions, discover solutions.

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:23.160
You've probably
heard a lot this week

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:25.920
about different kinds
of marketplace venues

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:30.510
that are out there to help make
your products discoverable.

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:34.230
And it's not sufficient anymore
to only make yourself available

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:37.260
in one venue, one
infrastructure provider, even.

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:41.550
On the dev side, we also
see that the actual dev

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:44.220
process is impacted by this.

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:46.800
Whether you're trying to package
solutions into the cloud,

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:51.610
or you need cloud-based building
blocks to create your solution.

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:53.670
If you use that old
enterprise procurement

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:56.490
model, where it's not
instant and on demand,

00:03:56.490 --> 00:03:58.830
it can elongate your
entire development cycle

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:01.450
and elongate your
go-to-market activities.

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:04.110
It also can restrict
your developers

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:09.910
from using the most innovative
and modern products.

00:04:09.910 --> 00:04:15.810
So having that click-to-purchase
brings back agility.

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:21.430
And having consumption-based
pricing helps lower costs.

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:25.720
And this should overall, if
we set all of these systems

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:29.350
up correctly, help to make
sure that devs are not

00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:31.300
hindered by the
inability to adapt

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:34.660
to quick, new,
emerging technologies.

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:36.550
Now, the marketplace
writ large--

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:39.700
I mean everyone here, you're
on day three of Google Next.

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:42.610
I don't need to convince you
that the cloud is some place

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:43.780
to be.

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:46.210
We all know that the
cloud is growing.

00:04:46.210 --> 00:04:49.720
But it has some very
important implications

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:53.170
about where software
sales models,

00:04:53.170 --> 00:04:56.600
and where stacks are going
to be deployed in the future.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:05:02.920
So in 2019, according to this
research study, about 1/3

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:04.900
of all enterprise
applications will

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:08.350
be cloud-only rather
than cloud-first.

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:12.420
Cloud-first is still
a big move today.

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:16.410
The industry is evolving
extremely rapidly.

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:21.460
83% of IT buyers rely on
product demos and lit.

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:23.987
They want that consumer-driven
cloud experience.

00:05:23.987 --> 00:05:26.320
And they want to get their
hands dirty with the solution

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:30.220
before they're willing to
actually go to all of the time

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:33.400
to architect their end-to-end
operational workflow

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:36.392
behind this cloud adoption.

00:05:36.392 --> 00:05:37.850
And when they get
those demos, they

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:43.090
are 50% more likely to
actually adopt a solution.

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:44.530
The industry is
growing, as well.

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:48.460
These gray bars in
the right-hand chart

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:52.210
are showing infrastructure
spending growth on the cloud.

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:56.350
What's not often discussed
is those blue bars.

00:05:56.350 --> 00:06:00.310
That's actual software
spend on the cloud.

00:06:00.310 --> 00:06:04.280
Specifically, SaaS and
PaaS-based offerings,

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:05.950
most of which have
to have some kind

00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:10.240
of consumption-based
pricing model behind them.

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:14.530
That software side of the curve,
lower than infrastructure.

00:06:14.530 --> 00:06:16.750
But it's still expected to
triple over the next five

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:17.410
years.

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:21.350
This is a massive
opportunity for ISVs today.

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:23.920
So what does this mean?

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:25.890
Well, it means if
you're not a cloud ISV,

00:06:25.890 --> 00:06:29.490
you're being disrupted by
your competition right now.

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:31.530
Plain and simple.

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:36.290
ISVs have to adapt to the
needs of their customers.

00:06:36.290 --> 00:06:40.910
Also, in the cloud, a lot
of channel or ecosystems

00:06:40.910 --> 00:06:44.830
have been left behind in the
direct marketplace model.

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:47.630
And ecosystems that
create network effects

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:51.720
of multiple partners,
creating multiple solutions,

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:54.690
are where you can get
true value and start

00:06:54.690 --> 00:06:57.510
to drag more partner
activity, as well

00:06:57.510 --> 00:06:59.640
as more end-customer activity.

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:04.780
It's a very virtuous,
self-fulfilling cycle.

00:07:04.780 --> 00:07:06.520
In order to create
this ecosystem,

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:09.090
you have to automate it.

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:13.890
Any kind of manual process
in cloud distribution

00:07:13.890 --> 00:07:16.380
slows things down a lot.

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:18.270
It's unnecessary friction.

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:21.180
So both Apigee and
Orbitera are really

00:07:21.180 --> 00:07:23.790
about enabling
automation, enabling

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:28.710
end-to-end integration,
to create ecosystems

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:33.840
that create virtuous cycles
of customer satisfaction

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:36.640
and partner engagement.

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:41.340
So let's talk a little bit
about Orbitera as a product.

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:46.350
I heard a product manager
from one of our partners

00:07:46.350 --> 00:07:49.020
earlier today, and
he said that Orbitera

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:50.760
has been talked
about it quite a bit

00:07:50.760 --> 00:07:52.095
over the course of the week.

00:07:52.095 --> 00:07:53.730
I'm not entirely
sure what it does,

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:54.780
but it seems like
if you sprinkle

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:57.321
a little Orbitera on it, it will
solve your billing problems.

00:07:59.890 --> 00:08:02.995
So let's actually dig
into what Orbitera is.

00:08:02.995 --> 00:08:05.240
Orbitera is an
e-commerce platform.

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:12.220
We try to bring entities on the
left, who are our customers--

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:13.840
and this can be
software vendors,

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:17.440
it can be distributors or
resellers, system integrators

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:19.630
that need different building
blocks to be combined

00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:22.600
into bundled solutions, or
managed service providers that

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:24.130
like to layer on
their own services

00:08:24.130 --> 00:08:26.022
on top of cloud solutions.

00:08:26.022 --> 00:08:27.730
All of these are
different customer types

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:31.490
that can be enabled with
the Orbitera platform.

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:34.900
And with that network
effect, or the ecosystem,

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:39.860
where Orbitera can create what
we call an n-tier hierarchy.

00:08:39.860 --> 00:08:45.620
We can scale an unlimited number
of tiers down, sideways, up.

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:48.800
And this allows for
flexible business models.

00:08:48.800 --> 00:08:56.160
And we try to bring those
entities on the left

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:57.930
to their customers on the right.

00:08:57.930 --> 00:09:01.600
And those customers on the
right might not be the end user.

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:04.540
From an ISV's perspective,
or distributor's perspective,

00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:07.180
the reseller of the
product is their customer.

00:09:07.180 --> 00:09:09.340
So they need to
enable their customer,

00:09:09.340 --> 00:09:14.700
from that perspective, to
have a more satisfying selling

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:16.680
and development experience.

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:18.529
So the middle of
the box is really

00:09:18.529 --> 00:09:20.820
talking about the different
Orbitera platform features.

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:24.180
The first row is really
our guiding principles,

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:26.801
where we want to
reduce friction.

00:09:26.801 --> 00:09:28.800
We want to package and
provision different kinds

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:33.180
of software, cloud providers,
access to different cloud

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:37.310
providers, through
native cloud automation.

00:09:37.310 --> 00:09:41.710
Whenever possible, enabling
single-click deployment.

00:09:41.710 --> 00:09:43.420
And with a whole
host of configurable

00:09:43.420 --> 00:09:47.200
workflows to help you scale your
business to the next billion

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:49.690
users.

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:52.560
The next three rows talk about
the different product lines

00:09:52.560 --> 00:09:54.870
underlying Orbitera.

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:56.480
And you can think
of these either a la

00:09:56.480 --> 00:09:58.300
carte or holistically.

00:09:58.300 --> 00:10:00.760
We have some partners
who use Orbitera

00:10:00.760 --> 00:10:04.030
mostly as a billing engine, some
who use us for a test drive,

00:10:04.030 --> 00:10:06.520
some as a white
label marketplace.

00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:09.220
But they can also be
used holistically.

00:10:09.220 --> 00:10:13.870
So billing allows us to
implement subscription

00:10:13.870 --> 00:10:16.870
or consumption-based
billing anytime

00:10:16.870 --> 00:10:19.300
we can get programmatic
access to that subscription

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:21.970
or consumption information.

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:27.400
We have native support for
GCP, as well as for AWS,

00:10:27.400 --> 00:10:30.430
for Microsoft Azure,
for IBM SoftLayer,

00:10:30.430 --> 00:10:35.050
for CenturyLink Cloud, more
than a dozen SaaS applications.

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:39.630
We can consume any kind of
metering or consumption stream.

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:42.030
And then, through
our price books,

00:10:42.030 --> 00:10:47.120
apply custom pricing to
either resellers or end users.

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:50.570
And wrapped around this is
Dashboard's reconciliation

00:10:50.570 --> 00:10:52.790
and reporting tools,
that allow you

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:56.000
to surface to your customers
a single pane of glass,

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:58.970
through which they can
consume their AWS, their GCP,

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:02.960
their Azure, their software,
their SaaS subscriptions--

00:11:02.960 --> 00:11:06.600
everything in one shop.

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:10.830
And we can deploy into
multiple cloud environments

00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:13.850
from that one marketplace.

00:11:13.850 --> 00:11:17.240
That leads us to the next row,
marketplaces and catalogs,

00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:20.380
where we can enable
our partners to create

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:23.860
their own e-commerce
white-label storefront.

00:11:23.860 --> 00:11:27.730
Looks and feels
like their domain,

00:11:27.730 --> 00:11:29.830
registered on
their domain space,

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:33.820
and hooked up with all of the
consumption and subscription

00:11:33.820 --> 00:11:37.120
pricing that's enabled by the
subscription management engine

00:11:37.120 --> 00:11:39.370
underlying Orbitera.

00:11:39.370 --> 00:11:44.460
And all of this, again,
is an n-tier hierarchy,

00:11:44.460 --> 00:11:45.690
an n-tier architecture.

00:11:45.690 --> 00:11:48.060
So we can enable
your channel partners

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:50.859
to stand up their own
white-label marketplaces,

00:11:50.859 --> 00:11:53.400
where they don't have to worry
about the underlying technical

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:55.550
integrations.

00:11:55.550 --> 00:11:58.490
Lastly, we have trials
and lead management,

00:11:58.490 --> 00:12:00.800
also known as test drives.

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:03.400
And this solution, as
well, is being integrated

00:12:03.400 --> 00:12:05.920
into multiple different
Google programs,

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:09.860
and is also available
on other clouds.

00:12:09.860 --> 00:12:12.840
The thin line wrapping
this whole diagram

00:12:12.840 --> 00:12:16.960
is speaking to Orbitera's
automation capabilities.

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:20.140
We want to reduce friction, not
increase systems complexity.

00:12:20.140 --> 00:12:23.680
So we have a rich framework
of callbacks and APIs

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:27.750
to automate integrations with
different kinds of systems.

00:12:27.750 --> 00:12:30.270
And ideally, that end
system is something

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:34.290
like Apigee, which is a unified
management platform that

00:12:34.290 --> 00:12:37.380
provides us a single
integration point to then speak

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:41.606
to all of the underlying
systems within an ISV.

00:12:41.606 --> 00:12:44.240
I'll get into that
in just a minute.

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:46.010
So how does Orbitera help?

00:12:46.010 --> 00:12:49.670
We try to help you grow revenue,
accelerate sales, and optimize

00:12:49.670 --> 00:12:51.530
operations.

00:12:51.530 --> 00:12:55.180
Specifically, we
help you grow revenue

00:12:55.180 --> 00:12:59.440
by enabling true
multi-cloud commerce.

00:12:59.440 --> 00:13:02.440
When I say that, I mean that
we actually meter and deploy

00:13:02.440 --> 00:13:04.060
into multiple clouds.

00:13:04.060 --> 00:13:07.150
We have the big three
public clouds today--

00:13:07.150 --> 00:13:10.690
Google Cloud, AWS, and Azure.

00:13:10.690 --> 00:13:15.800
And we can bundle multiple
infrastructure, as well as

00:13:15.800 --> 00:13:23.030
SaaS or license-based solutions,
into a single product that's

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:25.910
deployed through that
single-click framework.

00:13:25.910 --> 00:13:29.600
And we do that through the
native provisioning services

00:13:29.600 --> 00:13:31.190
of these different clouds.

00:13:31.190 --> 00:13:34.040
It also helps simplify
the purchase experience,

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:38.720
because it's a much more
consumer-driven kind

00:13:38.720 --> 00:13:42.320
of feel and workflow.

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:44.030
And through this,
you can actually

00:13:44.030 --> 00:13:48.960
customize consumption
pricing for any end user.

00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:53.240
It does not have to be
shared across users.

00:13:53.240 --> 00:13:56.210
Also, we have been
able to channel

00:13:56.210 --> 00:13:59.000
through that multi-tier
framework, where

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:01.670
every reseller can
have their own shingle,

00:14:01.670 --> 00:14:03.210
their own white-label
marketplace.

00:14:03.210 --> 00:14:05.300
They can put it on
their own domain space.

00:14:05.300 --> 00:14:10.160
And so long as a partner has
integrated with Orbitera,

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:12.020
or if they have their
own solutions that

00:14:12.020 --> 00:14:17.290
have some kind of API, or some
kind of scriptable deployment,

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:20.770
that reseller can inherit
those other products

00:14:20.770 --> 00:14:23.350
from past ISVs that
have integrated with us,

00:14:23.350 --> 00:14:25.540
or build their own solutions.

00:14:25.540 --> 00:14:29.200
It's a completely
self-service framework.

00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:32.110
And this really helps you
enable your partner base.

00:14:32.110 --> 00:14:35.800
Accelerating cloud sales
is about streamlining

00:14:35.800 --> 00:14:38.170
deployment, streamlining
access to solutions

00:14:38.170 --> 00:14:41.240
through test drives.

00:14:41.240 --> 00:14:44.210
And all of this is with an
eye towards automation--

00:14:44.210 --> 00:14:46.610
integrating with your
existing CRM system

00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:50.280
so that lead
generation is seamless,

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:53.760
so that your sales team can
help nurture these new leads.

00:14:53.760 --> 00:14:58.240
And we can actually
notify you in real time

00:14:58.240 --> 00:15:01.040
when a new lead has
accessed your test drive.

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:06.190
You can call them before the
environment has completed.

00:15:06.190 --> 00:15:07.870
In terms of
optimizing operations,

00:15:07.870 --> 00:15:11.930
this is really about automation.

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:15.100
If you have an API,
we can work with you.

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:18.140
If you don't have an API,
we can refer you to Apigee,

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:19.460
and then we can work with you.

00:15:19.460 --> 00:15:20.300
I'm just kidding.

00:15:20.300 --> 00:15:24.410
We can work with different kinds
of partner solutions, as well.

00:15:24.410 --> 00:15:26.820
Not necessarily API-driven.

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:30.530
We have some partners who
are just nascently entering

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:31.390
the cloud.

00:15:31.390 --> 00:15:32.960
And we have
implemented workflows

00:15:32.960 --> 00:15:34.950
through automated
email notifications.

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:37.550
We've done this through
automated notifications

00:15:37.550 --> 00:15:38.960
of different JSON endpoints.

00:15:38.960 --> 00:15:41.870
They're totally
end-to-end APIs where

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:44.951
Orbitera is a silent
partner in the background.

00:15:47.780 --> 00:15:51.160
And through our integrations
with different clouds,

00:15:51.160 --> 00:15:55.060
we help satisfy your
end users' needs.

00:15:55.060 --> 00:15:56.560
Because different
cloud providers

00:15:56.560 --> 00:15:58.960
have different features
and functionalities.

00:15:58.960 --> 00:16:00.250
It's not a bad thing.

00:16:00.250 --> 00:16:01.420
It's not a taboo.

00:16:01.420 --> 00:16:03.510
It's just reality.

00:16:03.510 --> 00:16:08.130
And so your partners demand to
be able to deploy and consume

00:16:08.130 --> 00:16:10.350
different clouds.

00:16:10.350 --> 00:16:13.540
Orbitera helps you enable that.

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:17.060
So now let's talk a
little bit about Apigee.

00:16:17.060 --> 00:16:20.620
Apigee is an API
management platform

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:27.690
that really helps streamline the
end-to-end digital value chain.

00:16:27.690 --> 00:16:29.970
One of the guiding
principles of Apigee

00:16:29.970 --> 00:16:32.100
is they have a very
opinionated view

00:16:32.100 --> 00:16:36.420
of what APIs can and should be.

00:16:36.420 --> 00:16:40.770
Specifically, it's not
sufficient to simply look

00:16:40.770 --> 00:16:43.940
at things from the back-end out.

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:47.930
You can't slap APIs
on top of everything

00:16:47.930 --> 00:16:51.980
and expect to have a unified
user experience, where

00:16:51.980 --> 00:16:55.730
the user on the far
left of this slide

00:16:55.730 --> 00:16:58.850
is being considered
from day one.

00:16:58.850 --> 00:17:00.920
So Apigee likes
to think of things

00:17:00.920 --> 00:17:06.410
both from an inside-out as well
as an outside-in perspective.

00:17:06.410 --> 00:17:08.750
Because it's not just
a matter of making sure

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:10.490
that your devs
are building APIs.

00:17:10.490 --> 00:17:13.160
You need to rationalize
all those APIs, make

00:17:13.160 --> 00:17:14.990
sure your different
dev teams are using

00:17:14.990 --> 00:17:18.440
the same kind of language.

00:17:18.440 --> 00:17:21.950
And through that, Apigee
can be the polyglot

00:17:21.950 --> 00:17:25.010
that does all the translations
between your different teams,

00:17:25.010 --> 00:17:29.180
wraps all these together,
scales, secures,

00:17:29.180 --> 00:17:32.660
and helps monetize these
different kinds of automated

00:17:32.660 --> 00:17:36.540
systems that you're enabling.

00:17:36.540 --> 00:17:42.070
So the Apigee platform,
or Apigee Edge,

00:17:42.070 --> 00:17:45.080
can be seen in many
different angles.

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:48.410
Whether you're the
app user, you're

00:17:48.410 --> 00:17:52.700
the operational team
monitoring and administering

00:17:52.700 --> 00:17:55.490
the back-end, whether you're
the developers or the API

00:17:55.490 --> 00:18:00.102
team trying to bring that
developed solution to your apps

00:18:00.102 --> 00:18:00.935
and to your systems.

00:18:03.174 --> 00:18:04.590
So here are some
of the principles

00:18:04.590 --> 00:18:08.310
of Apigee that you see on
the right-hand of this slide.

00:18:08.310 --> 00:18:14.010
Apigee is absolutely a
purpose-built, cloud-native API

00:18:14.010 --> 00:18:16.860
management platform, with
that centralized point

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:19.720
of government.

00:18:19.720 --> 00:18:23.620
Fully multi-tenant support,
just like Orbitera.

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:28.480
Apigee is a truly
multi-cloud platform

00:18:28.480 --> 00:18:30.712
that can be installed in
multiple cloud environments,

00:18:30.712 --> 00:18:31.420
and even on-prem.

00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:39.420
Again, much like Orbitera, they
take a self-service standpoint.

00:18:39.420 --> 00:18:41.970
Because the last
thing a partner needs

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:45.060
when they need nimbleness
and responsiveness is

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:48.150
to file a ticket with their
platform to actually make

00:18:48.150 --> 00:18:49.630
something happen.

00:18:49.630 --> 00:18:51.480
We want to put the
tools in your hands.

00:18:54.660 --> 00:18:59.340
And obviously, it's about
scaling to enterprise.

00:18:59.340 --> 00:19:02.640
And Apigee has helped
many enterprises

00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:05.250
deliver their applications,
their services,

00:19:05.250 --> 00:19:09.520
to millions and
millions of users.

00:19:09.520 --> 00:19:14.930
Here's some of the flavor behind
Apigee's deep integrations

00:19:14.930 --> 00:19:17.690
with multiple
cloud environments.

00:19:17.690 --> 00:19:20.990
As you can see here,
Apigee, while fully

00:19:20.990 --> 00:19:24.470
owned and integrated with
Google Cloud Platform,

00:19:24.470 --> 00:19:26.600
has also installed
their application

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:28.250
in multiple other environments--

00:19:28.250 --> 00:19:33.360
AWS, on Azure,
through Cloud Foundry,

00:19:33.360 --> 00:19:36.390
on GCP, and Kubernetes
environments, as well.

00:19:36.390 --> 00:19:40.730
And you can install Apigee
in an on-prem environment

00:19:40.730 --> 00:19:44.624
to help bridge that gap between
the reality of today, where

00:19:44.624 --> 00:19:46.040
you're not quite
yet on the cloud,

00:19:46.040 --> 00:19:47.748
and the future, where
you want to get to.

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:53.915
So how do these two
platforms fit together?

00:19:57.590 --> 00:20:02.180
Orbitera is a platform that
helps you monetize, bill,

00:20:02.180 --> 00:20:06.950
demonstrate, and distribute
your products, your solutions.

00:20:06.950 --> 00:20:11.600
Products can be bundles of
multiple apps or single apps.

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:14.660
And we help you create
ecosystems and link

00:20:14.660 --> 00:20:16.700
partnerships together.

00:20:16.700 --> 00:20:20.930
So if you're a distributor, you
can invite your ISV partners

00:20:20.930 --> 00:20:25.020
to publish their products into
your distributor ecosystem.

00:20:25.020 --> 00:20:27.980
Or if you're an ISV that
wants to enable that,

00:20:27.980 --> 00:20:30.350
you just need to integrate
with our systems,

00:20:30.350 --> 00:20:34.580
and you can use us as
a force multiplier.

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:40.450
Apigee is API
management at scale.

00:20:40.450 --> 00:20:44.380
That allows connections between
different user experiences,

00:20:44.380 --> 00:20:46.561
different end systems.

00:20:46.561 --> 00:20:48.310
And if you've ever
done a cloud migration,

00:20:48.310 --> 00:20:53.200
you know that it's real-- it can
be painful and onerous, trying

00:20:53.200 --> 00:20:56.230
to herd the cats of all
your different APIs.

00:20:56.230 --> 00:21:00.030
Apigee makes that process
relatively painless.

00:21:00.030 --> 00:21:02.910
When you combine these
two platforms together,

00:21:02.910 --> 00:21:05.640
Orbitera can act as
the unified front-end,

00:21:05.640 --> 00:21:08.920
with billing management,
partner management,

00:21:08.920 --> 00:21:11.074
ecosystem management
tools, as well as

00:21:11.074 --> 00:21:12.490
all of the reporting
and analytics

00:21:12.490 --> 00:21:16.270
that you might need, while
Apigee provides the automated,

00:21:16.270 --> 00:21:21.380
unified management portal
that Orbitera can speak with,

00:21:21.380 --> 00:21:24.060
and scale all of their
underlying systems

00:21:24.060 --> 00:21:28.370
to accelerate your
go-to-market activity.

00:21:28.370 --> 00:21:31.970
So let's go through a few
hypothetical examples.

