00:26:50.260 --> 00:26:52.870
so that Pitney
Bowes' admins have

00:26:52.870 --> 00:26:58.090
complete control over
what's published and where.

00:26:58.090 --> 00:27:00.840
We have the Android-powered
device on the left-hand side.

00:27:00.840 --> 00:27:05.680
We've been collaborating
closely with the Android team

00:27:05.680 --> 00:27:08.920
to create a
customized device that

00:27:08.920 --> 00:27:13.930
sits on top of this shipping
label machine, that can then

00:27:13.930 --> 00:27:16.240
be used by these
small businesses

00:27:16.240 --> 00:27:20.280
to purchase new
products and services--

00:27:20.280 --> 00:27:23.910
things like G Suite for
the small business--

00:27:23.910 --> 00:27:26.010
right through the
shipping label machine.

00:27:29.230 --> 00:27:33.520
Then, Orbitera itself enables
a myriad of pricing models

00:27:33.520 --> 00:27:36.239
within this ecosystem.

00:27:36.239 --> 00:27:38.280
You can pay by the sip,
you can pay by the drink,

00:27:38.280 --> 00:27:40.240
you can pay by the seat.

00:27:40.240 --> 00:27:42.700
Pay for it by the
week, month, year.

00:27:42.700 --> 00:27:44.440
Fortnight, too, if you want.

00:27:44.440 --> 00:27:47.400
You define the frequencies.

00:27:47.400 --> 00:27:51.990
And all of this is then
integrated with a seamless user

00:27:51.990 --> 00:27:52.710
experience.

00:27:52.710 --> 00:27:55.710
Because we need to have the
user experience in mind each

00:27:55.710 --> 00:27:57.240
and every step of the way.

00:27:57.240 --> 00:28:01.010
And very importantly, as Pitney
